# AGENT.md — src/core/

The innermost circle. Enterprise and application business rules.

## Absolute rules

- **Nothing here imports from `adapters/`, `modules/`, or `shared/`.**
  Source-code dependencies point inwards only. This is the rule that makes
  the business logic testable without a database or an HTTP server.
- No HTTP, no SQL, no ORM types. Use-cases speak in domain entities.
- Ports are interfaces the outer circles must implement — declare what the
  core needs, never how it is satisfied.

## What goes where

- `entities/` — enterprise business rules. The objects and their invariants.
- `use-cases/<module>/` — application business rules. One class per action,
  each exposing `execute()`.
- `ports/` — the interfaces (plus their DI tokens) that `adapters/` fulfils.

## Adding a use-case

Create the class in `use-cases/<module>/`, inject the port via
`@Inject(<MODULE>_REPOSITORY)`, then register it as a provider in
`src/modules/<module>.module.ts`. Never inject a concrete repository class.
